In article <JBW.93Jan28235109@bigbird.bu.edu>, jbw@bigbird.bu.edu (Joe Wells) writes:

> 1. How do you specify which window interface to use dynamically?  I have
>    to resort to editing the binary to switch between "tty" and "X11".

in your .nethackrc or your HACKOPTIONS environment variable, you can set
the option windowtype to be either x11 or tty.

> 2. Typeahead is ignored when the X11 popup is used.  This is most
>    noticeable when opening doors ("ol") and invoking extended commands
>    ("#l") and kicking ("^Dj").  It is annoying when you need to repeat an
>    action many times that asks for confirmation.

Yeah.  I think there needs to be something done about that.

> 3. The visibility rules seem to have some strange bugs.  I often see
>    things far away across the level that are only reachable through twisty
>    passages.  There is no straight line of sight to the things I am being
>    shown.

This isn't a bug.  I thought it was too, at first until I realized that
what's happening is that you're seeing into a lit room down a dark
corridor.  Because you have line of sight through the corridor you can
see into the room even though the corridor is too dark to see anything
in.

> 6. How do you set the number of lines remembered in the message window?
>    I'd like it to remember the last 1000.

There's a #define in winX.h called MAX_HISTORY which is currently set to 60.

> 10. The popup that lets you type text expands *very slowly* when you type
>     more text than will fit.  This is easily seen when wishing for the
>     neat stuff.

Get a faster machine.  :-)

